      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T16:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need a separate means of controlling the log level of u-boot. Bootconfig is for kernel and beyond, but for u-boot. uboot_env.img might be used for this.\n\nIt\u0027s not clear if u-boot has a dynamic log-level filtering mechanism. The existence of the CONFIG_LOGLEVEL config suggests that it\u0027s static..:( But I might be wrong.\n\nAnother problem is that reading and evaluating uboot_env.img is not the first thing that u-boot does. So we need to either *statically* silence any log (including u-boot version and fingerprint) prior to the point, or emit all the early logs anyway hoping that they don\u0027t put a pVM at risk.",
